text outside a template: template line 1: every line outside a '@template' must be blank -- a source is a sheet of named templates
a template with no name: template line 1: '@template' needs a name
two templates of one name: template line 4: this sheet already has a template called 't'
a template never closed: template line 1: template 't' is never closed by an '@end'
a nested template: template line 2: a '@template' cannot sit inside another one
a lone @: template line 2: a lone '@' -- write '@@' for a literal one, or '@{name}' for a hole
an unclosed hole: template line 2: '@{' with no closing '}'
an empty hole: template line 2: '@{}' names nothing
an unknown directive: template line 2: unknown directive -- the six are '@template', '@for', '@choose', '@when', '@otherwise', '@yield' and '@end'
an @for that eats the template @end: template line 1: template 't' is never closed by an '@end'
@choose with no @when: template line 2: a '@choose' with no '@when' chooses nothing
text before the first @when: template line 2: a '@when' has to follow '@choose' immediately -- there is text between them
two @otherwise: template line 2: this '@choose' has two '@otherwise' sections
an unknown template: this sheet has no template called 'nope' (it has: greet, pick, over)
an unbound hole: '@{name}' is not bound (bound: greeting)
a binding nothing uses: 'extra' is bound and template 'greet' never mentions it (it uses: greeting, name)
a tag no @when names: '@choose kind' is 'shouty', which no '@when' names (it has: loud, quiet)
a tag one does: ok -> quiet

@choose over rows: '@choose kind' is bound to a list of rows, and it holds a string
@for over a string: '@for .. in rows' needs rows, and 'rows' is bound to a string
a cell that is not there: '@{r.cell}' names no cell of that row (it has: other)
